  "articleBody": "When it comes to getting repairs done for a senior's home, it's easy to make a few common missteps that can lead to frustration or even shoddy work. One of the biggest mistakes is hiring someone based on an unsolicited offer, like a flyer on the door or a cold call. Always do your homework! Another common one is not checking references or credentials. Make sure you're working with someone reputable, like a BBB Accredited Business with an A+ rating such as HH Remodeling LLC. Don't pay too much upfront; a fair payment schedule means you pay as work progresses, not all at once before anything is even done. Failing to get a written contract is also a huge risk. This contract should clearly outline the scope of work, pricing, timeline, and any warranties. Without it, you're leaving a lot to chance. Also, make sure the contractor has experience with senior-specific needs and clear communication. Avoiding these pitfalls will help ensure your senior home repair project goes smoothly and safely. We prioritize clear communication and documented pricing, so you know exactly what to expect. Just give Abraham a call at 303-505-0866.",
